{
    "word": "magus",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "b30be77f-9cd5-30a1-8bbc-63630adc81ba",
                "word": "magus",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ea595560-6d8b-42c5-9e7b-0a3647082dac",
                        "entry_id": "b30be77f-9cd5-30a1-8bbc-63630adc81ba",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "magi"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "aa52f86e-168e-4a22-b50b-332cba12d8c6",
                        "entry_id": "b30be77f-9cd5-30a1-8bbc-63630adc81ba",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "form": "maguses"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f54a7583-9e37-354f-9a0a-d88a9232a9e4",
                        "entry_id": "b30be77f-9cd5-30a1-8bbc-63630adc81ba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A magician; (derogatory) a conjurer or sorcerer, especially one who is a charlatan or trickster."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "419f6932-63e4-4e17-8d0e-f9859645e813",
                                "sense_id": "f54a7583-9e37-354f-9a0a-d88a9232a9e4",
                                "text": "In the middle of the fifth century, Empedocles testified to the vitality of these maguses, who were capable of commanding the winds and of bringing the dead back from Hades and who presented themselves, not as mortals, but as gods."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e3f38907-8ead-4849-9d28-e9bb227dc549",
                                "sense_id": "f54a7583-9e37-354f-9a0a-d88a9232a9e4",
                                "text": "It’s from our venerable maguses Gominik Halvor and his son. They’ve cast the runes for our enterprise."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0b198b12-5ec9-345e-85a0-56c954e7ca94",
                        "entry_id": "b30be77f-9cd5-30a1-8bbc-63630adc81ba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A Zoroastrian priest."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a327cda-7b06-434c-97fd-90a032cc8d21",
                                "sense_id": "0b198b12-5ec9-345e-85a0-56c954e7ca94",
                                "text": "Court astrologers, who were drawn from the race of the Magi, were among those that formed the royal court [...]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a3de8e76-e063-4a77-8935-d12dad7cd4b3",
                                "sense_id": "0b198b12-5ec9-345e-85a0-56c954e7ca94",
                                "text": "Mocenigo / [satisfied at last] / Good! Now, tell me, Prior, / What is Rome’s greatest fear? What gives the Pope / More night-mares than bad sausage? / Prior Gabrielli / Heresy! / The rendering of the seamless robe of truth. / This rabble of mountebanks and maguses / Who shout reform, defile the Eucharist, / Flout all authority, elect false bishops, / Deny the Trinity and saving grace, / Abolish marriage, set their private minds / Against the long tradition of the Faith / And Peter’s dictates and the Holy Writ . . ."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a54e2529-efaa-4d44-97e9-b15173147b91",
                        "source_entry_id": "b30be77f-9cd5-30a1-8bbc-63630adc81ba",
                        "source_sense_description": "magician",
                        "target_lang_word": "mage",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mage",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b93b0cfa-3c77-37ef-b08a-df84efcdefba",
                                        "entry_id": "fa1004c3-a3d5-3fd2-ac22-dee779a74eaf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Prêtre de la religion de Zoroastre, chez les Perses et les Mèdes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd8abfc0-01a9-4dc6-879a-d52bc74accfa",
                                                "sense_id": "b93b0cfa-3c77-37ef-b08a-df84efcdefba",
                                                "text": "Il s'agit de la Perse primitive. Les textes, quoique confus, laissent pourtant distinguer trois âges, le patriarcal, celui où le prêtre apparaît, enfin l'âge où le magisme médo-caldéen se greffe sur la Perse. — Les mages ne furent pas proprement une caste, mais une tribu. Le magisme ne s'organise guère qu'après la conquête de Babylone."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ef10599c-c653-3c4b-b343-85c2d9633d99",
                                        "entry_id": "fa1004c3-a3d5-3fd2-ac22-dee779a74eaf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "L'un des Rois mages qui seraient venus de l’Orient à Bethléem pour adorer Jésus-Christ."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "especially"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81f055b8-2079-459e-aea7-3b2f02eefd23",
                                                "sense_id": "ef10599c-c653-3c4b-b343-85c2d9633d99",
                                                "text": "Sans remonter au Déluge, l'évaluation des récits bibliques à l’aune de la science ne date pas d'hier. Elle est même vieille comme Hérode. Mais l'« étoile » des Mages est sans doute l'évènement qui a le plus fait calculer les astronomes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "390177a3-4264-3870-8e03-a0bb58c2dff0",
                                        "entry_id": "fa1004c3-a3d5-3fd2-ac22-dee779a74eaf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Astrologue ; devin ; spécialiste des sciences occultes et de la prédiction de l’avenir."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a166cff0-2283-4d2d-92a2-70f74f9cbd97",
                                                "sense_id": "390177a3-4264-3870-8e03-a0bb58c2dff0",
                                                "text": "Après une violente dispute avec son mari, elle consulte un mage qui lui prédit un sombre avenir."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "mage",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "55a7bec8-f6df-3245-b18d-b314889db823",
                                        "entry_id": "166c083e-0103-3af8-888f-3dadcb8f50b7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Principal, plus grand."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3ca5124-4b96-41b9-ab80-33cb7c305a4b",
                                                "sense_id": "55a7bec8-f6df-3245-b18d-b314889db823",
                                                "text": "Finalement, voyant que tous estoient mors, getta le corps de Loup Garou tant qu'il peut contre la ville, et tomba comme une grenoille sus ventre en la place mage de ladicte ville, et en tombant du coup tua un chat bruslé, une chatte mouillée, une canne petiere, et un oyson bridé."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
